---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { layouts, pins, releases, themes, short } from '../data/product';

const shell = pins.shell;
const config = pins.config;
const hornero = pins.hornero;
const currentRelease = releases.find((release) => release.status === 'tagged');
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Roots — Hornero OS"
  description="How Hornero grew from a personal desktop configuration into an open operating-system project, with its sources and credits intact."
>
  <section class="intro section">
    <p class="eyebrow">An open project, with its history intact</p>
    <h1>
      Built from a desktop.
      <br />
      <em>Grown into a system.</em>
    </h1>
    <p>
      Hornero began as a personal configuration, then grew into a set of maintained projects for the shell, themes,
      operating-system tools, testing and documentation.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section timeline-section">
    <p class="eyebrow">How it grew</p>
    <h2>From dotfiles to HorneroOS</h2>
    <ol class="timeline">
      <li>
        <span class="timeline-mark">01</span>
        <div>
          <h3>A desktop takes shape in dotfiles</h3>
          <p>
            The personal Linux environment behind Hornero has been developed, used, refined and tested for more than
            eight years. Its public configuration continues in{' '}
            <a href="https://github.com/ulises-jeremias/dotfiles">ulises-jeremias/dotfiles</a>, alongside the broader
            Arch Linux setup it grew from.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="timeline-mark">02</span>
        <div>
          <h3>The shell becomes its own project</h3>
          <p>
            Hornero copied the shell into its own repository while preserving the original source and license. The
            migration replaced workstation-only paths with XDG-based configuration so installed packages can stand on
            their own.
          </p>
          <a href={`${shell.repo}/blob/${shell.sha}/NOTICE`}>
            Read the shell attribution and migration record <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="timeline-mark">03</span>
        <div>
          <h3>One shell, many arrangements</h3>
          <p>
            Earlier Polybar and Waybar configurations informed several familiar topologies. <em>Cockpit Clear</em> and{' '}
            <em>Islands</em> cite Polybar; <em>Cozy Minimal</em> and <em>Dock Bottom</em> cite Waybar. Today,{' '}
            <strong>{layouts.length} layouts</strong> arrange bars and islands through one Quickshell system and one
            shared preset format.
          </p>
          <a href="/layouts">
            Explore the current layouts <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="timeline-mark">04</span>
        <div>
          <h3>The operating system grows around it</h3>
          <p>
            Theme packs, <code>horneroctl</code>, the greeter, an installer contract and a dedicated QA repository give
            the desktop a path from source code to a tested system.
          </p>
          <a href="/releases">
            See the release history <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="section map-section">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Maintained in clear pieces</p>
      <h2>Every part has a home.</h2>
      <p>The repositories are separate so each layer can be reviewed, packaged and tested at the right boundary.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="repo-list">
      <a href={`${shell.repo}/tree/${shell.sha}`}>
        <span class="repo-mark">01</span>
        <span>
          <strong>Shell</strong>
          <small>Quickshell runtime, layout presets, Companion and shell services</small>
        </span>
        <code>{short(shell.sha)}</code>
      </a>
      <a href={`${config.repo}/tree/${config.sha}`}>
        <span class="repo-mark">02</span>
        <span>
          <strong>Config</strong>
          <small>Appearance packs, defaults, brand assets and package data</small>
        </span>
        <code>{short(config.sha)}</code>
      </a>
      <a href={`${hornero.repo}/tree/${hornero.sha}`}>
        <span class="repo-mark">03</span>
        <span>
          <strong>Hornero</strong>
          <small>Native CLI, release compositions and system capabilities</small>
        </span>
        <code>{short(hornero.sha)}</code>
      </a>
      <a href="https://github.com/HorneroOS/greeter">
        <span class="repo-mark">04</span>
        <span>
          <strong>Greeter</strong>
          <small>Hornero’s SDDM login screen and its Qt 6 runtime</small>
        </span>
        <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
      <a href="https://github.com/HorneroOS/installer">
        <span class="repo-mark">05</span>
        <span>
          <strong>Installer</strong>
          <small>Staged installation contract; a public ISO is not available yet</small>
        </span>
        <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
      <a href="https://github.com/HorneroOS/qa">
        <span class="repo-mark">06</span>
        <span>
          <strong>QA</strong>
          <small>Virtual-machine journeys and evidence for complete product builds</small>
        </span>
        <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section lineage" id="community">
    <p class="eyebrow">Influence, credit and direction</p>
    <h2>Learn from good work. Keep our own shape.</h2>
    <div class="lineage-grid">
      <article>
        <h3>Code ancestry</h3>
        <p>
          The Quickshell shell is adapted from <a href="https://github.com/caelestia-dots/shell">Caelestia Shell</a>.
          The upstream author, license and imported commit remain documented in the repository.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Design references</h3>
        <p>
          <a href="https://github.com/Ryoku-dev/ryoku">Ryoku</a>,{' '}
          <a href="https://github.com/AvengeMedia/DankMaterialShell">DankMaterialShell</a> and{' '}
          <a href="https://github.com/omacom/omarchy">Omarchy</a> help us study how other teams make settings
          discoverable, themes coherent and Linux desktops approachable.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Hornero’s direction</h3>
        <p>
          Those references inform the questions we ask, not the answers we copy. Hornero keeps its own visual range,
          open development and product decisions.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>People behind HorneroOS</h3>
        <p>
          <a href="https://github.com/ulises-jeremias">Ulises Jeremías</a> is HorneroOS’s principal maintainer.{' '}
          <a href="https://github.com/PandaFoss">Panda Foss</a> contributes to the project and maintains the{' '}
          <a href="https://gitlab.com/anarchyinstaller/installer">Anarchy Installer</a>; that experience informs
          HorneroOS’s installer work. Both are part of the{' '}
          <a href="https://github.com/HorneroOS">HorneroOS organization</a>. Panda has been working on the
          Calamares-based installer intended as HorneroOS's official installation path and will lead its future custom
          installer work.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="source-line">
      Sources checked at Shell{' '}
      <a href={`${shell.repo}/commit/${shell.sha}`}>
        <code>{short(shell.sha)}</code>
      </a>
      , Config{' '}
      <a href={`${config.repo}/commit/${config.sha}`}>
        <code>{short(config.sha)}</code>
      </a>{' '}
      and Hornero{' '}
      <a href={`${hornero.repo}/commit/${hornero.sha}`}>
        <code>{short(hornero.sha)}</code>
      </a>
      . The pinned sources define {themes.length} theme packs
      {currentRelease && (
        <>
          {' '}
          and include the tagged composition <a href={`/releases#${currentRelease.name}`}>{currentRelease.name}</a>
        </>
      )}
      .
    </p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .intro {
    padding-block: clamp(1rem, 4vw, 4rem) 1.5rem;
  }
  .intro h1 {
    margin-top: 0.7rem;
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 2rem + 5vw, 6.2rem);
    line-height: 0.98;
    letter-spacing: -0.055em;
  }
  .intro h1 em {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-style: normal;
  }
  .intro > p:last-child {
    max-width: 59ch;
    margin-top: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
  }
  .timeline-section > h2,
  .map-section h2,
  .lineage > h2 {
    margin-top: 0.4rem;
  }
  .timeline {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0;
    max-width: 850px;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .timeline li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 3.2rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 1.35rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .timeline-mark,
  .repo-mark {
    color: var(--secondary);
    font: 0.75rem var(--font-data);
  }
  .timeline h3 {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
  }
  .timeline p {
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .timeline a {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .map-section {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    padding: clamp(1.3rem, 4vw, 2.6rem);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--surface);
  }
  .map-section > div:first-child > p:last-child {
    margin-top: 0.55rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .repo-list {
    display: grid;
  }
  .repo-list > a {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2rem 1fr auto;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    min-width: 0;
    padding: 0.9rem 0.1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--text);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .repo-list strong,
  .repo-list small {
    display: block;
  }
  .repo-list small {
    margin-top: 0.12rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .repo-list code {
    color: var(--secondary);
  }
  .repo-list a:hover strong {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .lineage-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.8rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .lineage-grid article {
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--surface);
  }
  .lineage-grid p {
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .source-line {
    margin-top: 1.4rem;
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
  }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .map-section {
      grid-template-columns: 0.7fr 1.3fr;
      align-items: start;
    }
    .lineage-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
</style>
